cc
Usage: sh ~/tools/xexec -t ~/tools/cc cc FILE.c -o OUT

Compiles C right on the stick: `cc` is tcc with its own preprocessor, assembler
and linker plus a musl sysroot, producing a static binary with no external
toolchain. For a quick proof-of-concept or a small tool in the field.

	cc file.c -o out        compile to a named output
	cc file.c -o out && ./out   build and run it
	-static                 force a fully static link (the default here)

See also: python, xexec, radare2
